# Editing Guidelines

Use these durable content practices.
Use `AGENTS.md`, `editing-cycle.md`, and `release.md` for workflow, validation, and Package.
Sections above ## Project Practices are govna-maintained canon and update via canon syncs; repo-specific practices in ## Project Practices.

## Cross-Reference Integrity

- When a doc references another file, section, or heading, verify the target exists before publishing
- When renaming or moving a file, grep the repo for all references and update them in the same pass
- When deleting a section or heading, check for inbound links from other docs

## Link Integrity

- Internal links use repo-relative paths
- External links include the full URL
- Verify links are not stale before publishing
- Flag broken links as findings during review

## Structural Conventions

- Use consistent heading hierarchy within each document
- Do not skip heading levels (e.g., jump from `##` to `####`)
- Keep one topic per file
- Split files that cover unrelated concerns
- Use flat `##` sections with inline bullets
- Avoid deep nesting unless structure genuinely requires it

## Formatting Rules

- Prefer plain text and simple bullets over tables or rich formatting unless content clearly benefits
- Use code fences for file paths, commands, and configuration values
- Keep lines readable — no hard wraps at arbitrary column widths, but avoid single-paragraph walls of text
- Use consistent terminology throughout the repo
- Define each term in one place
- Reference the canonical definition

## Documentation Alignment

- Ship docs with content changes.
- Verify referenced paths and headings.
- Update every affected doc in one pass.
- Propagate shared governance changes across source and flavor-equivalent overlay documents.

## Project Practices

- Follow existing repo patterns unless an approved improvement says otherwise.
